  "notes": [
    "The Burmese (Myanmar) script for SquirrelGo Alphabets. Romanization is a simplified common style (hs for the breathy s, ht and hp for aspirates, th for θ). Each consonant's hint gives its traditional name. eSpeak NG reads Burmese letters poorly, so the sounds are made from the IPA, without tones. Hints, groupings and articles are original."
